<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow> breaks `sf`
        deploy at source conversion with the misleading error "unable to find matching parent
        xml file". Precedent in this repo: flows/Counter_Offer_Notify.

        WHAT THIS FLOW IS. A BEFORE-SAVE record-triggered flow that projects the fine-grained
        Negotiation_Status__c onto the coarse Stage__c, which is a DERIVED field: a direct write
        to Stage__c COMMITS AND IS SILENTLY DISCARDED (measured org behaviour, recorded in both
        Contract_Review__c record type files). This flow is therefore the ONLY place the coarse
        stage can be changed.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-14 (Phase 3, observation 7, requirements C4). IT NOW KNOWS 'Draft'.
        THIS IS A DEFECT FIX, NOT AN ENHANCEMENT - WITHOUT IT PHASE 3 SHIPS BROKEN AND GREEN.
        =====================================================================

        THE DECISION Map_Status HAS A DEFAULT CONNECTOR AND NO RECORD-TYPE CRITERION, so it
        serves BOTH PSA record types and anything it does not recognise falls through to
        Stage__c = 'Review'. Acquisition_PSA's sequence becomes
        Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed. Left alone, 'Draft' would have hit that
        default and a BRAND-NEW acquisition PSA would have opened showing coarse
        Stage__c = 'Review' instead of 'PSA Drafting' - on its first save, on every deal, with a
        green deploy and no error anywhere.

        🔴 'Initial Draft' IS KEPT, NOT REPLACED, AND THAT IS THE HARD CONSTRAINT. Disposition_PSA
        still runs Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready for Execution -> Executed and is untouched by
        Phase 3 (decision O3). Swapping the literal instead of adding one would move the identical
        defect onto the sell-side path. The two rules are therefore SEPARATE and both connect to
        Set_Stage_Drafting - the duplicate-entry shape this repo prefers over an OR, for the same
        reason LOI_Record_Page and NDA_Record_Page use it: a single rule with two conditions and
        conditionLogic '1 OR 2' would work here, but two named rules read as two vocabularies and
        can be deleted independently when Disposition_PSA is eventually migrated.

        ⚠ 'Negotiation' AND 'Signed' ARE DELIBERATELY LEFT TO THE DEFAULT CONNECTOR. They are the
        exact analogues of 'Revised' and 'Ready for Execution', which also fall to it and project
        to 'Review'. That is CORRECT, not an omission: the coarse stage has only three values
        (PSA Drafting / Review / Contract Execution) and the middle of either sequence is
        'Review'. 🔴 DO NOT "improve" this by projecting 'Signed' to 'Contract Execution' - that
        would move the Transactions handoff a step early. ONLY 'Executed' reaches
        Contract Execution, and ContractExecutionService keys on 'Executed' too.
        🔴 THIS PARAGRAPH IS PARTIALLY RETRACTED 2026-08-21 - see the dated block below. It
        remains fully correct for ACQUISITION_PSA. It stopped being correct for Disposition_PSA
        the moment that record type's terminal became 'Signed' rather than 'Executed'.

        ⚠ RULE ORDER MATTERS - the first matching rule wins. Is_Draft is placed immediately after
        Is_Initial_Draft and before the two Executed rules; the values are mutually exclusive, so
        the placement is for readability rather than correctness, but keep the two Executed rules
        LAST in that relative order (the date-stamping one before the date-kept one) because
        THOSE two overlap and their order IS load-bearing. The new Is_Disposition_Signed rule
        added 2026-08-21 is placed AFTER both Executed rules and does not reorder them; it cannot
        overlap either (Negotiation_Status__c cannot simultaneously equal 'Executed' and 'Signed'),
        so its position relative to them is for readability only, same as Is_Draft's.

        ⚠ THIS FIX MUST BE DEPLOYED BEFORE THE PHASE 3 ROW MIGRATION, not with the Apex. The
        migration writes Initial Draft -> Draft on every acquisition Contract Review, and this is
        a before-save flow, so it fires on every one of those rows. If it does not yet know
        'Draft', the migration itself stamps coarse Stage__c = 'Review' across the whole live
        acquisition population - a data defect, not just a rendering one. The edit is purely
        additive and is correct on both sides of the migration, so it ships at P3-D1.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-21. THE USER CHANGED Disposition_PSA.Negotiation_Status__c DIRECTLY IN
        SETUP THE SAME DAY (full measurement in the record type file's own header). DISPOSITION_
        PSA'S TERMINAL IS NOW 'Signed', NOT 'Executed', AND THE "LEAVE 'Signed' TO THE DEFAULT"
        PARAGRAPH ABOVE - WRITTEN WHEN 'Signed' WAS NEVER A TERMINAL FOR EITHER RECORD TYPE - NO
        LONGER COVERS THAT CASE CORRECTLY.
        =====================================================================================

        RETRACTED, in part, from the paragraph above: "'Negotiation' AND 'Signed' ARE DELIBERATELY
        LEFT TO THE DEFAULT CONNECTOR. They are the exact analogues of 'Revised' and 'Ready for
        Execution', which also fall to it." That was true of 'Signed' only while Disposition_PSA
        could never hold it. It can now, and it is that record type's TERMINAL, not its analogue
        of a mid-sequence status - so 'Signed' is no longer one thing for the purposes of this
        decision, it is two, depending on which record type carries it.

        NOT RETRACTED - STILL BINDING FOR ACQUISITION_PSA: "DO NOT 'improve' this by projecting
        'Signed' to 'Contract Execution' - that would move the Transactions handoff a step early."
        On Acquisition_PSA, 'Signed' still precedes 'Executed', which is still the only value that
        triggers ContractExecutionService's handoff. A blanket edit that made 'Signed' project to
        'Contract Execution' for BOTH record types would be wrong for acquisition and is NOT what
        was built.

        THE FIX - A NEW, NARROWLY-SCOPED RULE, NOT A CHANGE TO THE DEFAULT. Is_Disposition_Signed
        tests Negotiation_Status__c = 'Signed' AND Disposition__c IS NOT NULL, and routes to the
        EXISTING Set_Stage_Executed_Only assignment (Stage__c = 'Contract Execution', no other
        field touched). Reusing that assignment rather than adding a new one is deliberate: its
        behaviour - set the coarse stage, stamp nothing else - is exactly what this case needs,
        and 'Signed' is not literally 'Executed' so Execution_Date__c must NOT be stamped here (
        that stays owned by the acquisition-only Set_Stage_Executed / Is_Executed_Needs_Date pair,
        which this new rule does not touch). Acquisition rows never match the new rule's second
        condition (Opportunity__c is what OpportunityReviewService stamps on them; Disposition__c
        stays blank, per Disposition_PSA's own record type header), so 'Signed' still falls to the
        unchanged default connector for every acquisition row, exactly as before.

        🔴 THE DISCRIMINATOR IS Disposition__c, NOT RecordType.DeveloperName - DECIDED ON THE
        MERITS, NOT BY DEFAULT. 'Signed' cannot be exempted by NAMING A VALUE the way
        flows/NDA_Signed_Status_Sync exempts the acquisition NDA terminal (its 'Declined' is
        exposed on Disposition_NDA only; this object's 'Signed' is exposed on BOTH record types
        now, so no value-naming trick is available - see that flow's own header for why a
        value-named exemption is preferred WHEN one exists). Absent that option, the lookup is
        still preferred over RecordType.DeveloperName for the same two measured reasons that flow
        and flows/PSA_Ready_Notify both record: (1) a record-type test silently skips MASTER-type
        Contract Reviews, the shape TestDataFactory produces when a record type is absent from or
        unavailable in a scratch org - RecordStageAdvanceService still carries a null/Master
        fallback for this exact object; (2) a record-type test breaks on a record type rename,
        a value/lookup test does not. Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c's sibling field
        Opportunity__c is not this object's own header's words, but the identical rule is already
        stated for this object family on Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c's own field header:
        "THE LOOKUP, NOT THE RECORD TYPE, IS THE DISCRIMINATOR anything outside the record page
        should test."

        CONSERVATIVE BY CONSTRUCTION: this is an ADDITIVE rule appended after the two existing
        Executed rules. No existing rule, connector, assignment or the default connector was
        edited, removed or reordered. Is_Initial_Draft, Is_Draft, Is_Executed_Needs_Date and
        Is_Executed_Dated are BYTE-IDENTICAL to before this change.
    -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Stage_Drafting</name>
        <label>Set Stage Drafting</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Stage__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>PSA Drafting</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Stage_Executed</name>
        <label>Set Stage Executed</label>
        <locationX>302</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Stage__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Contract Execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Execution_Date__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Flow.CurrentDate</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Stage_Executed_Only</name>
        <label>Set Stage Executed (date kept)</label>
        <locationX>428</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Stage__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Contract Execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Stage_Negotiation</name>
        <label>Set Stage Review</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Stage__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Review</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <decisions>
        <name>Map_Status</name>
        <label>Map Negotiation Status</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>180</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Set_Stage_Negotiation</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Reviewing</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Initial_Draft</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Negotiation_Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Initial Draft</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Stage_Drafting</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Initial Draft</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Draft</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Negotiation_Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Draft</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Stage_Drafting</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Draft (Acquisition_PSA)</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Executed_Needs_Date</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Negotiation_Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Executed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Execution_Date__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Stage_Executed</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Executed - stamp date</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Executed_Dated</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Negotiation_Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Executed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Stage_Executed_Only</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Executed - date kept</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Disposition_Signed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Negotiation_Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Signed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Disposition__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Stage_Executed_Only</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Signed (Disposition_PSA terminal)</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Contract Review Stage Sync {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Contract Review Stage Sync</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Map_Status</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Negotiation_Status__c</field>
            <operator>IsNull</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Contract_Review__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordBeforeSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
